# Throwaway probe scripts and specs (MAINTAINING.md names the convention), so a stray
# `git add -A` can't ship one.
*-tmp.*
# …and the same, for the prefix the review agents actually use. The `-tmp.` convention only
# protects a session that remembers it: on 2026-08-09 two verification agents wrote
# `e2e/zzprobe.spec.ts` and `e2e/zzprobeB.spec.ts` while a gate was running, a `git add -A`
# minutes later swept both in, and they reached `main`. A convention nothing enforces is a
# convention that holds until the one time it matters.
zz*.spec.ts
zz*-probe.*

# Written by scripts/stamp-version.mjs at build time so the deployed site can say
# which commit it is. Generated, never committed — a checked-in copy would be stale.
/public/version.json

/node_modules
/.next
/out
/build
/playwright-report
/test-results
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
.vercel
.env*.local

# Private flight-log corpus fetched by scripts/fetch-fixtures.mjs (never committed).
# Both forms: the fetched directory, and a symlink to a local checkout of the
# fixtures repo (the trailing-slash pattern alone does not match a symlink).
/lib/parsers/__corpus__
/lib/parsers/__corpus__/

# A stray build artefact once reached the repo root of a public repo (see BACKLOG, 2026-08-09).
a.out
*.o
